arm64: dts: r4-pro: 10G WAN AS21010P (gmac1 USXGMII), no kernel reset-gpios

gmac1 USXGMII to the AS21010P (phy28 @ MDIO 0x1c). No reset-gpios in the kernel
DT on purpose: phylib cannot drive a clean reset for this firmware-loading PHY
(as21xxx sets PHY_DETACH_NO_HW_RESET, and the reset-gpios are only ever acquired
deasserted), so the PHY is reset in u-boot board_late_init instead (see the
u-boot z13-bpirouter-wan-phy-reset patch) and Linux always probes a freshly
reset PHY that then reloads its firmware. The c45-id byte-swap seen during
bring-up is a MediaTek MDIO read artifact (unrelated to reset), handled by the
read-twice workaround (kernel 985/986); the mdio scan is delayed (kernel 997)
so the c45 id is ready when get_phy_c45_ids probes it.
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts
@@ -201,6 +201,44 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&eth {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&mdio0_pins>;
+};
+
+&gmac1 {
+	phy-mode = "usxgmii";
+	phy-connection-type = "usxgmii";
+	phy-handle = <&phy_10g_wan>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdio_bus {
+	/* AS21010P 10G WAN PHY at 0x1c. No reset-gpios here: phylib can't cleanly
+	 * reset this firmware PHY, so it is reset in u-boot (board_late_init, see
+	 * u-boot z13). The c45-id byte-swap is an MTK MDIO read artifact (985/986),
+	 * not reset; the mdio scan is delayed (kernel 997) for c45-id readiness. */
+	phy_10g_wan: ethernet-phy@1c {
+		compatible = "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c45";
+		reg = <0x1c>;
+		firmware-name = "as21x1x_fw.bin";
+	};
+};
+
+&pio {
+	mdio0_pins: mdio0-pins {
+		mux {
+			function = "eth";
+			groups = "mdc_mdio0";
+		};
+	};
+
+	wan_combo_copper_hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <3 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-low;
+	};
+};
 &i2c2 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c2_1_pins>;
